cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research prototype, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "VISTA: artifact-grounded structural verification of exported ML models with Lean"
authors:
  - given-names: "Anuj"
date-released: 2026-07-29
version: "0.1.0"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >
  VISTA checks whether structural facts derived from an exported
  machine-learning artifact are sufficient to instantiate selected formal
  requirements, expressed as Lean theorems, under explicit interface and
  external assumptions -- emitting an artifact-bound certificate whose
  formal theorem application is checked by the Lean kernel. VISTA is a
  pre-training structural verifier: it never uses a trainable parameter's
  values as verification evidence. A density-functional-theory case study
  (self-adjointness, long-range coupling, exchange-correlation
  discontinuity) is included as a broader formalization example, not as
  the project's primary claim.
